# Phase 1 — Rename `assignee_id` → `owner_id`

Spec item 6: "the field `assignee_id` is renamed `owner_id` everywhere."

## Context

`assignee_id` is set and read in `src/tickets.js` only; nothing in `src/portal.js`, `src/notify.js`, or
`src/jobs/close-resolved.js` / `purge-closed.js` touches it. The one place a rename has an outside consequence is
`src/jobs/export-tickets.js:3`, whose output file is "picked up by the finance team's reporting job, which that
team deploys on its own schedule" — an external API contract (hot path). Production backs the same store
interface with Postgres, so this is also, in effect, a column rename there; that migration is out of this repo
and out of scope for this plan, but someone on the data/infra side needs to run it before this ships, and the
temporary export alias below is what buys the time to coordinate it.

